          "worked": "Read each whisker endpoint for the minimum and maximum, each box edge for a quartile, and the line inside each box for the median.\n\nIn the order minimum, lower quartile, median, upper quartile, maximum:\n\nChannel A: approximately $7,\\ 10.5,\\ 15,\\ 16.3,\\ 23$.\n\nChannel B: approximately $7.8,\\ 11,\\ 14.6,\\ 16.7,\\ 25$.\n\nChannel C: approximately $8,\\ 10,\\ 13,\\ 14.5,\\ 16$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Which channel has the largest interquartile range?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Channel A (approximately equal to Channel B).",
          "worked": "Using the approximate quartiles:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{IQR}_A&=16.3-10.5=5.8\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}_B&=16.7-11=5.7\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}_C&=14.5-10=4.5\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThese readings give Channel A the largest interquartile range, although the boxes for A and B are almost equal in width.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If the winning channel is the one with the highest rated program, which channel is the winner? Which is second? Which is third?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "First: Channel B; second: Channel A; third: Channel C.",
          "worked": "Compare the maximum ratings at the right-hand whisker endpoints: Channel B has approximately $25$, Channel A $23$ and Channel C $16$.\n\nThe ranking is B, A, C.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If the winning channel is the one with the largest median, rank the channels.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "First: Channel A; second: Channel B; third: Channel C.",
          "worked": "Compare the median lines: Channel A has approximately $15$, Channel B $14.6$ and Channel C $13$.\n\nThe ranking is A, B, C.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q11-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Can you find a criterion that makes Channel C the winning channel?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Sample answer: the channel whose lowest-rated program has the highest rating.",
          "worked": "Use the highest minimum rating as the criterion. Channel C's minimum is approximately $8$, compared with $7.8$ for Channel B and $7$ for Channel A, so Channel C wins.",
